    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization on owner create so the app satisfies the spec and both acceptance tests (`coreStripsToTenDigits`, `errorRejectsTooFewDigits`) pass.\n\nThe challenge was that the telephone value is validated in two layers before reaching business logic. My changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 The generated `OwnerFieldsDto` had bean validation `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'`, which would have rejected formatted input like `(04) 1234-5678` with a 400 *before* any normalization could run. I relaxed the pattern to `'^[-0-9()+.\\s]*$'` so raw formatted numbers pass DTO validation and reach the controller for normalization.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After the required-fields check, it now normalizes the telephone via a new `normalizeTelephone` helper: strips every non-digit character (`\\D`), requires exactly 10 digits, and stores that 10-digit value on the DTO before mapping/saving. A non-10-digit result throws `InvalidFieldsException`. (This is scoped to create only, per the spec; `updateOwner` is untouched.)\n\n3. **`InvalidFieldsException`** (new) + a handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 mirrors the existing `RequiredFieldsMissingException` idiom to render a `400 Bad Request` with the offending field name under the `errors` property.\n\nThe `Owner` entity's existing `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` / `@Digits` constraints are left in place as defense-in-depth \u2014 the normalized 10-digit value satisfies them on persist.",
